# Baseline security headers for STATIC files (ADR 0006 WS-1): /assets/*, /live-sw.js,
# /models/*, manifests, icons. Cloudflare doesn't promise to apply this file to a Pages
# Function's response, and every page load (/, /live, the Stream Studio host) runs through
# functions/_middleware.ts — so the pages' CSP, Permissions-Policy, COOP and framing rules
# are set THERE, per app (Stream Studio vs the comic / chat app), overriding anything from
# here, with reports going to the /csp-report Function (never /api/*, so the backend
# container stays asleep).
#
# No CSP here on purpose: a module worker (the YAMNet sound model at /assets/yamnet.worker-*.js)
# takes its CSP from its own script response, so a policy on /* would reach inside the worker.
# HSTS has no `preload` until the owner confirms every subdomain serves HTTPS (owner action #6).
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: payment=(), usb=(), serial=(), hid=()

# Installable-app manifest: revalidate so name/icon/shortcut changes reach installs.
/app.webmanifest
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# App icons: stable names (regenerated by scripts/gen-icons.mjs), so a day of cache
# then revalidate rather than immutable.
/icons/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, stale-while-revalidate=604800

# Baby-monitor alert service worker: always revalidate so fixes reach phones.
/live-sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache

# On-device AI models (baby-monitor sound model). Versioned file names → cache forever.
/models/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
